-- Residential Tenancies Act 1986 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are worked from the Act's text and the 2026 calendar
-- (Easter Sunday 5 April 2026; Waitangi Day Friday 6 February; Anzac Day
-- Saturday 25 April, so Monday 27 April; the King's Birthday 1 June; Matariki
-- Observance Day 10 July; Labour Day 26 October), never from running the
-- code.

§ `Tests`

cal MEANS `Local calendar` OF (LIST Date 10 7 2026), (LIST Date 19 1 2026)
none MEANS `Local calendar` OF EMPTY, EMPTY

§§ `Working days (s 2)`

#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 6 2 2026) cal
#ASSERT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 9 2 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 27 4 2026) cal
#ASSERT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 28 4 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 3 4 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 6 4 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 7 4 2026) cal
#ASSERT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 8 4 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 1 6 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 26 10 2026) cal
#ASSERT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 19 10 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 24 12 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 3 1 2027) cal
#ASSERT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 4 1 2027) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 10 7 2026) cal
#ASSERT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 10 7 2026) none
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 19 1 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day under s 2` (Date 17 10 2026) cal

§§ `Deemed service (s 136)`

-- Posted Friday 16 October: the 4th working day is Thursday 22 October.
#ASSERT `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (Date 16 10 2026) `, served` `by post` `, calendar` cal EQUALS Date 22 10 2026
-- Posted Thursday 22 October: Labour Day is skipped, so Thursday 29 October.
#ASSERT `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (Date 22 10 2026) `, served` `by post` `, calendar` cal EQUALS Date 29 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (Date 21 12 2026) `, served` `by delivery to a mailbox or door` `, calendar` cal EQUALS Date 23 12 2026
-- Delivered Tuesday 22 December: the 2nd working day is Monday 4 January.
#ASSERT `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (Date 22 12 2026) `, served` `by delivery to a mailbox or door` `, calendar` cal EQUALS Date 4 1 2027
#ASSERT `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (Date 16 10 2026) `, served` `by email or other electronic address, after 5 pm` `, calendar` cal EQUALS Date 19 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (Date 16 10 2026) `, served` `by email or other electronic address, by 5 pm` `, calendar` cal EQUALS Date 16 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day a notice is deemed given, sent` (Date 16 10 2026) `, served` `personally` `, calendar` cal EQUALS Date 16 10 2026

§§ `Application (ss 5, 7, 8)`

periodicT MEANS Tenancy OF `none of the s 5 exclusions`, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, 0
holidayT MEANS Tenancy OF `holiday premises`, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, 0
#ASSERT `the Act applies to` periodicT
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to` holidayT
#ASSERT `the Act applies to` (Tenancy OF `holiday premises`, TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, 0)
#ASSERT NOT `sections 25 to 28 and 51 apply to` (Tenancy OF `none of the s 5 exclusions`, FALSE, JUST 60, TRUE, 60)
#ASSERT `sections 25 to 28 and 51 apply to` (Tenancy OF `none of the s 5 exclusions`, FALSE, JUST 60, TRUE, 120)
#ASSERT `sections 25 to 28 and 51 apply to` (Tenancy OF `none of the s 5 exclusions`, FALSE, JUST 60, FALSE, 60)
#ASSERT `sections 25 to 28 and 51 apply to` periodicT

§§ `Bonds (ss 18-22A)`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of bond`, amount IS A NUMBER, pet IS A BOOLEAN, agreed IS A BOOLEAN, held IS A BOOLEAN, security IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Bond demand`
bond k amount pet agreed held security MEANS `Bond demand` OF k, amount, 600, pet, agreed, held, security

#ASSERT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a general bond` 2400 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a general bond` 2401 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a pet bond` 1200 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a pet bond` 1201 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a pet bond` 1200 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a pet bond` 1200 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 18AA(2): one pet bond at a time, however many pets.
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a pet bond` 600 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the bond` (bond `a general bond` 2400 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the most further bond after a rent increase, kind` `a general bond` `, weekly rent from` 600 `to` 650 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the most further bond after a rent increase, kind` `a pet bond` `, weekly rent from` 600 `to` 650 EQUALS 100

-- Paid Friday 16 October: 23 working days, skipping Labour Day, end on
-- Thursday 19 November.
#ASSERT `the last day to lodge the bond, payment` (`Bond payment` OF Date 16 10 2026, NOTHING, FALSE, 4) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 19 11 2026)
#ASSERT `the bond was lodged in time` (`Bond payment` OF Date 16 10 2026, JUST (Date 19 11 2026), FALSE, 4) cal
#ASSERT NOT `the bond was lodged in time` (`Bond payment` OF Date 16 10 2026, JUST (Date 20 11 2026), FALSE, 4) cal
#ASSERT NOT `the bond was lodged in time` (`Bond payment` OF Date 16 10 2026, NOTHING, FALSE, 4) cal
#ASSERT `the last day to lodge the bond, payment` (`Bond payment` OF Date 16 10 2026, NOTHING, TRUE, 1) `, calendar` cal EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day to lodge the bond, payment` (`Bond payment` OF Date 16 10 2026, NOTHING, TRUE, 2) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 19 11 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day for a bond application without agreement by` `a landlord` `, tenancy ended` (Date 31 10 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2026)
#ASSERT `the last day for a bond application without agreement by` `a tenant` `, tenancy ended` (Date 31 10 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Rent (ss 23-30)`

#ASSERT `the landlord may require the rent in advance` (`Rent demand` OF 2, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the rent in advance` (`Rent demand` OF 3, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the landlord may require the rent in advance` (`Rent demand` OF 3, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the rent in advance` (`Rent demand` OF 1, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the landlord may require the rent in advance` (`Rent demand` OF 1, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)

GIVEN given IS A DATE, takes IS A DATE, started IS A DATE, last IS A MAYBE DATE, fixed IS A BOOLEAN, permits IS A BOOLEAN, boarding IS A BOOLEAN, order IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rent increase notice`
increase given takes started last fixed permits boarding order MEANS
    `Rent increase notice` OF given, takes, TRUE, started, last, fixed, permits, boarding, order, 650

-- Notice given 1 March 2026: 60 days end on 30 April.
#ASSERT `the earliest day the increase may take effect, notice` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2025) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS Date 30 4 2026
-- Changed after the independent pass: the anniversary of the start is within
-- the 12 months (fork F2), so the tenancy here starts on 29 April 2025, and
-- an increase on the anniversary is unlawful.
#ASSERT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 29 4 2025) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2025) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 29 4 2026) (Date 29 4 2025) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
-- Within 12 months of the start of the tenancy.
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 5 2025) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
-- Within 12 months of the last increase (1 June 2025).
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
-- Changed after the independent pass (fork F2): 1 June 2026 is the
-- anniversary of the last increase, so too early; 2 June is the first lawful
-- day.
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING)
-- A boarding house tenancy: 28 days.
#ASSERT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 29 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST 640))
#ASSERT `the rent increase is lawful` (increase (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST 650))

#ASSERT `the market rent application is in time` (`Market rent application` OF Date 15 4 2026, TRUE, Date 15 1 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the market rent application is in time` (`Market rent application` OF Date 16 4 2026, TRUE, Date 15 1 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the market rent application is in time` (`Market rent application` OF Date 16 4 2026, TRUE, Date 15 1 2026, JUST (Date 1 3 2026), NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the market rent application is in time` (`Market rent application` OF Date 16 4 2026, TRUE, Date 15 1 2026, NOTHING, JUST (Date 20 3 2026))
#ASSERT `the market rent application is in time` (`Market rent application` OF Date 16 4 2030, FALSE, Date 15 1 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING)
#ASSERT `a market rent order made on` (Date 1 5 2026) `may take effect on` (Date 31 5 2026) `, applied for on` (Date 10 4 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `a market rent order made on` (Date 1 5 2026) `may take effect on` (Date 1 6 2026) `, applied for on` (Date 10 4 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `a market rent order made on` (Date 1 5 2026) `may take effect on` (Date 9 4 2026) `, applied for on` (Date 10 4 2026)

#ASSERT `the receipt rules were met` (`Rent payment` OF `in cash`, TRUE, NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the receipt rules were met` (`Rent payment` OF `in cash`, FALSE, JUST 1)
#ASSERT `the receipt rules were met` (`Rent payment` OF `by another means needing a receipt`, FALSE, JUST 72)
#ASSERT NOT `the receipt rules were met` (`Rent payment` OF `by another means needing a receipt`, FALSE, JUST 73)
#ASSERT `the receipt rules were met` (`Rent payment` OF `by automatic payment or non-negotiable cheque from the tenant's account`, FALSE, NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the last day to keep the record of a payment on` (Date 16 10 2026) EQUALS Date 31 3 2034
#ASSERT `the last day to keep the record of a payment on` (Date 10 2 2026) EQUALS Date 31 3 2033
#ASSERT `the last day to keep the record of a payment on` (Date 1 7 2016) EQUALS Date 31 3 2024

§§ `Damage (ss 49A, 49B) and s 56B rent`

GIVEN intentional IS A BOOLEAN, careless IS A BOOLEAN, insured IS A BOOLEAN, lost IS A BOOLEAN, irr IS A BOOLEAN, cost IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Damage facts`
damage intentional careless insured lost irr cost MEANS `Damage facts` OF intentional, careless, cost, insured, lost, 500, irr, 600, 700

#ASSERT `the tenant's liability for the damage` (damage FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3000) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the tenant's liability for the damage` (damage FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3000) EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT `the tenant's liability for the damage` (damage FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3000) EQUALS 2400
#ASSERT `the tenant's liability for the damage` (damage TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3000) EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the tenant's liability for the damage` (damage FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 3000) EQUALS 2800
#ASSERT `the tenant's liability for the damage` (damage FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 300) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the tenant's liability for the damage` (damage FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3000) EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `the rent for the 2 weeks after the withdrawal, rent` 2000 `, tenants before` 4 `, remaining` 3 `, excluded` FALSE EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the rent for the 2 weeks after the withdrawal, rent` 2000 `, tenants before` 4 `, remaining` 3 `, excluded` TRUE EQUALS 2000

§§ `Termination by notice`

GIVEN who IS A `Who gives notice`, k IS A `Kind of tenancy`, g IS A `Ground for notice`, sent IS A DATE, how IS A `Means of service`, vacate IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination notice`
notice who k g sent how vacate MEANS `Termination notice` OF who, k, g, sent, how, vacate, TRUE, NOTHING

-- 90 days from personal service on 2 March 2026 end on 31 May.
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the landlord` `periodic` `s 51(1) the landlord, in any case` (Date 2 3 2026) `personally` (Date 31 5 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 31 5 2026)
#ASSERT `the termination notice is lawful` (notice `the landlord` `periodic` `s 51(1) the landlord, in any case` (Date 2 3 2026) `personally` (Date 31 5 2026)) cal
#ASSERT NOT `the termination notice is lawful` (notice `the landlord` `periodic` `s 51(1) the landlord, in any case` (Date 2 3 2026) `personally` (Date 30 5 2026)) cal
-- 42 days, posted Friday 16 October (deemed given 22 October): 3 December.
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the landlord` `periodic` `s 51(2)(b) an unconditional sale needs vacant possession` (Date 16 10 2026) `by post` (Date 3 12 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 3 12 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the tenant` `periodic` `s 51(2A) the tenant, in any case` (Date 16 10 2026) `by email or other electronic address, by 5 pm` (Date 6 11 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 6 11 2026)
-- A tenant cannot use the landlord's ground, and s 51 is for periodic tenancies.
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the tenant` `periodic` `s 51(1) the landlord, in any case` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 6 11 2027)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `the termination notice is lawful` (notice `the tenant` `fixed-term` `s 51(2A) the tenant, in any case` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 6 11 2027)) cal
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the tenant` `fixed-term` `s 56B withdrawal following family violence` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 18 10 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 18 10 2026)
-- s 56C (added after the independent pass): posted on Friday 16 October, it
-- is given that day, not on the 4th working day.
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the tenant` `fixed-term` `s 56B withdrawal following family violence` (Date 16 10 2026) `by post` (Date 18 10 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 18 10 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the tenant` `periodic` `s 56B withdrawal following family violence` (Date 16 10 2026) `by delivery to a mailbox or door` (Date 18 10 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 18 10 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the landlord` `fixed-term` `s 58A a build-to-rent fixed term of at least 10 years` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 18 12 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the tenant` `fixed-term` `s 58A a build-to-rent fixed term of at least 10 years` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 18 12 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 11 12 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the landlord` `fixed-term` `ss 59, 59A, 59B the premises are destroyed, uninhabitable or contaminated` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 23 10 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 23 10 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the tenant` `periodic` `ss 59, 59A, 59B the premises are destroyed, uninhabitable or contaminated` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 18 10 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 18 10 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (notice `the landlord` `periodic` `s 53(5) the service tenant died and a replacement is urgently needed` (Date 16 10 2026) `personally` (Date 21 10 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 21 10 2026)
-- s 53(3): not before the service contract ends.
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (`Termination notice` OF `the landlord`, `periodic`, `s 53(1) the service contract has ended or notice of its end was given`, Date 1 11 2026, `personally`, Date 30 11 2026, TRUE, JUST (Date 30 11 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (`Termination notice` OF `the tenant`, `periodic`, `s 53(1) the service contract has ended or notice of its end was given`, Date 1 11 2026, `personally`, Date 30 11 2026, TRUE, JUST (Date 10 11 2026)) `, calendar` cal EQUALS JUST (Date 15 11 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `the termination notice is lawful` (`Termination notice` OF `the landlord`, `periodic`, `s 51(1) the landlord, in any case`, Date 2 3 2026, `personally`, Date 31 5 2026, FALSE, NOTHING) cal

§§ `Termination by the Tribunal (ss 55, 55A, 56)`

GIVEN arrears IS A NUMBER
      rent IS A LIST OF Occasion
      anti IS A LIST OF Occasion
      filed IS A DATE
      remedied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Termination application`
app arrears rent anti filed remedied MEANS `Termination application` OF filed, TRUE, arrears, rent, anti, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, remedied, FALSE

-- Three late payments: due Monday 2 March (5th working day 9 March, paid 10
-- March), Monday 13 April (5th working day 20 April, paid 21 April), Monday
-- 25 May (the King's Birthday makes 2 June the 5th working day; paid 3 June).
o1 MEANS Occasion OF Date 2 3 2026, JUST (Date 10 3 2026), Date 10 3 2026
o2 MEANS Occasion OF Date 13 4 2026, JUST (Date 21 4 2026), Date 21 4 2026
o3 MEANS Occasion OF Date 25 5 2026, JUST (Date 3 6 2026), Date 3 6 2026
o3paid MEANS Occasion OF Date 25 5 2026, JUST (Date 2 6 2026), Date 3 6 2026
#ASSERT `rent was owing for at least 5 working days on` o1 cal
#ASSERT NOT `rent was owing for at least 5 working days on` (Occasion OF Date 2 3 2026, JUST (Date 9 3 2026), Date 10 3 2026) cal
#ASSERT NOT `rent was owing for at least 5 working days on` o3paid cal
#ASSERT `the Tribunal must terminate under s 55` (app 0 (LIST o1, o2, o3) EMPTY (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE) cal
#ASSERT NOT `the Tribunal must terminate under s 55` (app 0 (LIST o1, o2, o3) EMPTY (Date 2 7 2026) FALSE) cal
#ASSERT NOT `the Tribunal must terminate under s 55` (app 0 (LIST o1, o2, o3paid) EMPTY (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE) cal
#ASSERT `the Tribunal must terminate under s 55` (app 21 EMPTY EMPTY (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE) cal
#ASSERT NOT `the Tribunal must terminate under s 55` (app 20 EMPTY EMPTY (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE) cal
#ASSERT NOT `the Tribunal must terminate under s 55` (app 21 EMPTY EMPTY (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE) cal

-- s 55A: three occasions; the first and third 89 days apart, then 90.
a1 MEANS Occasion OF Date 2 3 2026, NOTHING, Date 3 3 2026
a2 MEANS Occasion OF Date 10 4 2026, NOTHING, Date 11 4 2026
a3 MEANS Occasion OF Date 30 5 2026, NOTHING, Date 31 5 2026
a3late MEANS Occasion OF Date 31 5 2026, NOTHING, Date 1 6 2026
#ASSERT `the Tribunal must terminate for anti-social behaviour` (app 0 EMPTY (LIST a1, a2, a3) (Date 20 6 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Tribunal must terminate for anti-social behaviour` (app 0 EMPTY (LIST a1, a2, a3late) (Date 20 6 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Tribunal must terminate for anti-social behaviour` (app 0 EMPTY (LIST a1, a2, a3late, Occasion OF Date 5 6 2026, NOTHING, Date 6 6 2026) (Date 20 6 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the last day to remedy under a s 56 notice given on` (Date 1 10 2026) `, allowing` 14 `days` EQUALS Date 14 10 2026

